y that we're talking  about right now  is what ultimately led the three players  and your princess  to drop out of twitch rivals now on july  13th  a few days after tuesday posted his  response your princess released a  short one-page statement clarifying a  few things in light of the growing  backlash against her  i was very naive instead of pushing to  resolve the issue offline  i posted my original statement online i  was not painting tuesday  to be a rapist or abuser nor was i  trying to cancel him  what i was trying to point out was i was  put in a situation that made me feel  very uncomfortable  flirting is not an open invitation to be  touched and often times women are blamed  and gossiped about in ways that can feel  earth-shattering at the time  end quote alright that was everything  that happened in july that started  all of this controversy now leading  through the next five months  up until now whenever your princess  would tweet  or just be on social media in general  people would be in her replies demanding  an apology  or calling her a liar and then riot  announced on december 15th  that your princess would be playing in  an upcoming league of legends all-stars  event  people still pissed off over what they  saw as false accusations and a lack of  an apology  were pissed off all over again that riot  would choose to include someone with  this kind of controversy hanging over  them  and then a few days after that because  of course there's always more documents  your princess put out a 15-page response  to the response tuesday put out  five months ago in july and just to  hammer this point home all of this  controversy  is seen as the reason why mike young  dragoon  and ll stylish refused to play with your  princess  and dropped out of twitch rivals but  let's get back to your princess's latest  document  she says that she was quiet over the  last five months since july  due to all of the backlash she was  getting from the community  she apologized for